        "body": "hi,\r\n\r\nI have a model from a BioTac, and I've converted the mesh into a .msh file. However, when I try to open the simulator using ./simulate and drag the XML file into the simulator, it shows a long loading time, and eventually, there's no response.\r\n\r\nHere is the XML code:\r\n```xml\r\n<mujoco model=\"soft\">\r\n  <option timestep=\"0.01\" integrator=\"implicitfast\" solver=\"CG\"/>\r\n\r\n  <worldbody>\r\n    <light diffuse=\".5 .5 .5\" pos=\"0 0 5\" directional=\"true\" dir=\"0 0 -1\" />\r\n\t  <geom name=\"floor\" type=\"plane\" size=\"10 10 10\" pos=\"0 0 0\" rgba=\"1 1 1 1\" />\r\n    <flexcomp name=\"softbody\" type=\"gmsh\" dim=\"3\" rgba=\".8 .2 .2 1\" radius=\"0.001\" pos=\"0 0 .3\" mass=\"10\" scale=\"1 1 1\" file=\"int_ext_skin_combined_ftw.msh\">\r\n        <edge equality=\"true\"/>\r\n    </flexcomp>\r\n  </worldbody>\r\n</mujoco>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe .msh file contains 4,246 vertices and 15,410 faces. Could the issue be caused by the data size being too large? Has anyone encountered the same problem? How much memory would be required for this? I was able to load it successfully on Colab, but calculating certain scenarios, such as falling, takes an extremely long time.\r\n\r\n.msh file:\r\n[int_ext_skin_combined_ftw.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17084718/int_ext_skin_combined_ftw.zip)\r\n\r\n\r\nyifan\r\n",
