        "body": "## Backgroud\r\n- I am making a synthetic tool for robot training, the physics engine is mujoco \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b79713ef-c30f-4993-87f4-574750d9c969\r\n\r\n- Render engine using self-developed realtime raytracing(same tech from issac)\r\n- It was great when the whole scene is built with rigid body\r\n- But when it cames to soft body\uff0cthe performance can not be realtime and has some bug\r\n- Here is the real scene what I want to achieve\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/75608369-7a9c-4b94-8edb-2307c5ce64ce\r\n\r\n## Sample Scene\r\n- To demonstrate it I wrote a simple soft scene with only one tetrahedron below\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/48790ef5-f2aa-456e-9116-f3a0059ef2b1\r\n\r\n- And I use fTetWild to tedrahetralize the tiger mesh as [the official doc told](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#body-flexcomp-element)\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9fd4e6be-97d9-483b-90ea-71761bfb9f26\r\n\r\n- The video shows the performance is not acceptable, and the tiger mesh never falls down to the groud\r\n- Here is the origin scene data - [softbody.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17096499/softbody.zip)\r\n\r\n## Question\r\n- \u2460 Am I doing right for building such kind of tedrahetra mesh to simulate?\r\n- \u2461 How to make it faster?\r\n- \u2462 Is there any plan to optimize performance for soft body simulation?\r\n- \u2463 If I using other soft body algorithm to replace mujoco's, is this feasible?\r\n",
